WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:06.443
Press a fingertip on the edge of a coin, and hold it still.

2
00:00:07.283 --> 00:00:09.223
What keeps telling your brain where that edge is?

3
00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:14.127
Some nerve fibres from that skin fire only while the skin is moving.

4
00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:15.947
Then they go quiet.

5
00:00:16.967 --> 00:00:19.307
Others keep firing for as long as you hold.

6
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:24.107
One such class is the slowly adapting type I afferent, or SA1.

7
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:29.850
In macaque fingertips, its firing carried the spatial layout of millimetre-scale

8
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.090
features, such as raised patterns.

9
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.760
Its firing has two parts.

10
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.800
First, a fast burst as the press begins.

11
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.000
That is the dynamic phase.

12
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.800
Then firing through the hold, with irregular gaps between spikes.

13
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.820
That is the static phase.

14
00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:51.973
Now the surprise. The cell that helps make the hold is not a neuron.

15
00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:54.387
It is the Merkel cell.

16
00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:59.107
In mice, it comes from epidermal progenitors, not from neural crest.

17
00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:04.627
In hairy mouse skin, Merkel cells cluster in touch domes beside guard hairs.

18
00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:09.167
An afferent's branched ending makes disc-like contacts on them.

19
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.480
So force can reach this fibre by two routes.

20
00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:15.493
The ending makes its own Piezo2.

21
00:01:16.433 --> 00:01:19.133
Even without Merkel cells, it still responds to touch.

22
00:01:20.166 --> 00:01:25.346
Or the Merkel cell feels force through its own Piezo2, and passes the signal across

23
00:01:25.346 --> 00:01:26.346
a synapse.

24
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.760
Predict. One route reports change.

25
00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:31.840
One route holds the press.

26
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.200
Which would you guess holds the press?

27
00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:43.573
In mouse touch domes, the ending mainly carries the onset.

28
00:01:44.473 --> 00:01:46.373
The Merkel cell mainly holds the press.

29
00:01:47.383 --> 00:01:49.243
That is the idea for this lesson.

30
00:01:50.163 --> 00:01:54.083
The ending mainly feels the change, and the Merkel cell mainly holds the press.

31
00:01:58.066 --> 00:01:59.546
This is mouse hairy skin.

32
00:02:00.426 --> 00:02:01.646
And the word mainly matters.

33
00:02:02.486 --> 00:02:04.646
The Merkel cell may help with the onset too.

34
00:02:05.666 --> 00:02:07.626
Rat whiskers give a different reading.

35
00:02:08.706 --> 00:02:12.306
There, another laboratory argues that Merkel cells drive both phases.

36
00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:18.630
Keep this. Two receptors feed one nerve, and each mainly makes one phase.
